          "inputProfile": "interval",
          "expected": "[{{u}},{{v}}]"
        }
      ],
      "solutionReview": {
        "headline": "Critical zeros split the number line into sign intervals.",
        "reasoning": [
          "The quadratic factors as ${{a}}(x-({{u}}))(x-({{v}}))$.",
          "Because the leading coefficient is positive, the quadratic is nonpositive between its two zeros.",
          "The ≤ symbol includes both zeros."
        ],
        "answerSummary": "$[{{u}},{{v}}]$"
      },
      "attemptFeedback": [
        "Do not decide the interval before finding both zeros; they are the sign-change boundaries."
      ],
      "supportHints": [
        "Factor or otherwise solve the related quadratic equation first, then use the sign of an upward-opening parabola."
